From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kent Tamura <tkent@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:35:25 -0700
Subject: Pass extracted TLD to CompactEncDet::DetectEncoding()

Previously, DetectTextEncoding() passed the full URL string from
hint_url.GetString() as the third argument (url_hint) to
CompactEncDet::DetectEncoding(). Because CompactEncDet::ExtractTLD()
does not strip userinfo ("user:pass@") when parsing a URL, a colon in
the userinfo (e.g. "http://a.jp:x@example.com/") caused ExtractTLD()
to treat the username as the host and extract a spoofed TLD hint.

The third argument of CompactEncDet::DetectEncoding() accepts either a
full URL or a bare top-level domain name (TLD). Extract the TLD from
hint_url.Host() in DetectTextEncoding() and pass only the TLD string
to avoid URL parser differentials.

Fixed: 578671521
Change-Id: Iaa37ffdbc310f9962e585e293c9e533e948610a0
